  "note": "Inlined dynamic-import namespaces in the background bundle whose declaration lands AFTER their first read, keyed as base-name{sorted exports} so Rollup's $N suffix shifts do not read as churn, and measured on the pre-minify capture (node_modules/.cache/gero/background.pre-minify.js) because terser mangles the names. All current entries are LATENT: every read sits inside a function, so they only bite if bundle evaluation aborts partway and leaves later consts uninitialised while already-registered listeners stay live. That is how login died with \"Cannot access 'midnightSync_service' before initialization\". This list may only shrink; a new entry fails the build. Six entries are here on purpose and should not be converted to static imports: ledger, ledger9 and the wallet-sdk-unshielded-wallet index are imported by midnightLedger.ts, which is shared with the options bundle where that dynamic import splits a 10 MB wasm chunk; midnightLedger9 and midnightShieldedLedger9 are cycle-breakers (their closures import their importers); midnightPrivateSync8 stays lazy so midnightPrivateSyncSession does not drag walletStore/storeMessagingBg (which touch `chrome` at module init) into its import-time footprint. History: converting one dynamic import to static reorders the bundle and can push another module into the hazard (midnightWalletStatePersistence, once), so re-measure after every conversion rather than assuming. Two entries left this list when the declaration lookup was anchored on Rollup's /*#__PURE__*/ annotation: until then a namespace emitted under a bare base name was matched against the first `const <name> =` anywhere in a 13 MB bundle, so @walletconnect/core (emitted as `index`, behind `const index = reader.readInt();`) and the i18n language list (emitted as `config`, behind `const config = this.config;`) were read ~24k and ~161k lines before their declarations and reported as safe. Both are fixed at the source rather than pinned - the two WalletConnect SDK imports are static (the iife never split them anyway) and i18n.config.ts moved out of the globbed locale directory. Finally: these keys are computed from bundled dependency code, so a node_modules that has drifted from package-lock.json invents offenders as fixed and introduced. Reproduce any failure after `npm ci` before treating it as a code change.",
